From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 124/124] PC5: 16-bit pictures on the Vulkan renderer, and every
 keyboard read (Wine patch 0904)

- 0904: a 16-bit back buffer presents through an 8-bit Vulkan swapchain, so a DirectDraw game's 16-bit full-screen mode works with Alternative.
- A USB keyboard is read at each of the system's indexes 0 to 3, the keys held on any of them together: a wireless mouse's receiver that is a keyboard too, plugged in first, took index 0, and the real keyboard was never read.
